<https://github.com/john1hsu/business-knowledge-graph/id/adverse-selection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The tendency, when one side of a market privately knows its own risk or quality before contracting, for a single average price to attract disproportionately the high-cost or low-quality types, shrinking or even unravelling the market; firms respond by screening, signaling, pooling and mandates." .
