<https://github.com/john1hsu/business-knowledge-graph/id/michael-c-jensen> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "American financial economist (1939–2024) at the University of Rochester and Harvard Business School who co-authored the 1976 agency-cost theory of the firm with William Meckling, introduced Jensen's alpha for fund performance, founded the Journal of Financial Economics and co-founded SSRN; his ideas shaped equity-based executive pay, leveraged buyouts and the shareholder-value movement." .
