<https://github.com/john1hsu/business-knowledge-graph/id/scenario-planning> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A strategic-planning practice, pioneered at Royal Dutch/Shell in the late 1960s and early 1970s, in which managers build a small set of internally consistent, plausible stories about how the business environment could unfold and use them to test strategies and challenge their own assumptions, rather than relying on a single forecast." .
