<https://github.com/john1hsu/business-knowledge-graph/id/switching-costs> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The one-time costs a buyer incurs when moving from its current supplier to a rival, such as learning, set-up, contractual penalties or lost relationships; they lock customers in, shape \"bargain-then-ripoff\" pricing and act as a barrier to entry and a source of supplier power." .
